<newsitem itemid="115378" id="root" date="1996-10-14" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Premier Farnell H1 pretax profit falls.</title>
<headline>Premier Farnell H1 pretax profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to July 28</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		16.0		   vs 17.0</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 5.2		    vs 4.37</p>
<p> Pretax		     56.1		   vs 71.3</p>
<p> Turnover		   442.3		  vs 264.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Above earnings per share adjusted to exclude rationalisation costs and other exceptional items. Unadjusted earnings per share was 13.6p vs 36.2p.  </p>
<p> Net taxed		  37.1		   vs 51.7</p>
<p> Attributable	     30.0		   vs 51.7</p>
<p> Pay date		   Dec 2</p>
<p> Div registration date  Oct 29</p>
<p> Ex-div date		Oct 21</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 57.5 to 63.1 million stg, with the consensus at 61.6 million.</p>
<p>Dividend forecasts for the electronic components distributor ranged from 5.0p to 5.5p, with the consensus at 5.0p.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
